6|0@microgrowery^1439905685#cu70kyl:VolkspanzerIsME$:Kill it, kill it with fire. And be very gentle while doing so. It looks far enough along to be able to pollinate whatever is within range. My advice would be to gingerly take a large garbage bag and drop it down over the plant and cinch tight before you cut. But, yes, that is totally a dude. And as far as making butter, don't bother. The distinguished gentleman before me stated the truth in that the male's produce no thc. Sorry for your loss, but at this point you need to cause a little damage as possible in reference to wanton pollination, unless thousands of seeds is what your going for...
8|0@microgrowery^1439907065#cu71akp:smokeNtoke1$:I've been looking for a while and can't find anything scientific, but most of the seasoned growers and mj book writers I've come across seem to think there are low amounts of THC in males. My own experience aside, I don't think you should be telling people that males produce no THC.
-3|0@microgrowery^1439915791#cu76t0z:VolkspanzerIsME$:That may be true, but in my experience the only useful thing a male is good for is pollination. Anything else is a waste of time and resources and keeping a male around for any length of time risks accidental pollination and the seeding of otherwise good sensimillia. There probably is trace amounts of thc in males, but not enough to do anything useful. That is why the fed allows hemp production. hemp is just the male cannabis plant processed for its fibers. 
6|0@microgrowery^1439918445#cu78moc:OortCloudCanna$:Hemp is most definitely not just "male cannabis plants." There is more than "trace" thc production in males, somewhere in the vicinity of what you'd expect from sugar leaf on a female, it's just not worth growing out because of the detrimental effect on any females in the room with the male(s). If you've only got one plant and its male you may as well grow it out and blast for hash instead of killing it unless you're worried about dragging pollen from that plant into another room with females. 
9|0@microgrowery^1439907735#cu71o4o:quadmachine$:Male plants do produce THC https://www.unodc.org/unodc/en/data-and-analysis/bulletin/bulletin_1971-01-01_1_page006.html However I will not risk my other plants getting polinated by this male in order to gain some potential edibles or hash, just not worth the risk..
